# OpenLeet AI - Frontend Design & Code Guidelines

## Visual & Aesthetic Standards
- **Theme:** Dark mode first. Use a sleek, minimalist developer palette (Zinc background `bg-zinc-950`, card surfaces `bg-zinc-900/80`, borders `border-zinc-800/80`).
- **Accents:** Use subtle, professional accents like Emerald (`text-emerald-450` for success/correctness) or Indigo/Violet for AI states.
- **Typography:** Inter or system sans-serif. Clean hierarchy (bold headers, muted descriptions `text-zinc-400`).
- **Spacing & Motion:** Generous padding (`p-4` to `p-6`), smooth transitions (`transition-all duration-200`), and subtle hover states (`hover:bg-zinc-800/50`).

## Component Rules
- Always use `shadcn/ui` components for modals, dropdowns, and tabs. Never write custom raw inputs or ugly unstyled buttons.
- Always use `lucide-react` for icons.
- For code previews, always use `@monaco-editor/react` with a dark theme (vs-dark) configured to match the app background.
